  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 249 PM CDT Wed Aug 5 2026\n\nNo changes to the forecast once again. Expect mid-level high \npressure to dominate the period. Expect this to promote warm and \nmostly rain free conditions outside of seabreeze convection. Some\nspotty showers have been popping up with the arrival of the\nseabreeze this afternoon. This is thanks to some midlevel energy\nriding the periphery of the ridge combining with the seabreeze. \nThese will continue to be isolated in nature and will diminish \nthis evening. Will continue to monitor the need for some short- \nfused heat related products. We could see heat indices up to 115 \nat times with dew points around the mid to upper 70s present \nthrough the next week. This translates to Moderate to Major heat \nstress conditions though we could see some areas reach Extreme \nconditions by Thursday. We strongly encourage the practice of heat\nsafety in these conditions. Take frequent breaks and remember to \nstay hydrated, check those backseats, and avoid long exposure in \nthese temperatures. For more information be sure to check out \nweather.gov/heatsafety.",
